            <ArticleTitle>Hip pain in children.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1018-21</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Children who present with a limp and pain in the hip, anterior thigh and the knee can have a serious disorder of the hip. The age at presentation tends to provide a guide to the possible problem, such as a slipped upper femoral epiphysis and a stress fracture of the femoral neck in adolescents.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
